From: Jake Hoffman <122403457+jakethehoffer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:01:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] build: add QNX detection and link libsocket and libfsnotify

On QNX the BSD socket calls (accept4(), ...) are exported by libsocket.so.4
and the inotify calls by libfsnotify.so.1, not by libc. <sys/socket.h> and
<sys/inotify.h> declare them, but a program that does not link the two
libraries gets undefined references.

The same is true for the configure-time probes (FLB_HAVE_ACCEPT4,
FLB_HAVE_INOTIFY, FLB_HAVE_UNIX_SOCKET): their test programs fail to link
unless both libraries are in CMAKE_REQUIRED_LIBRARIES, so the features are
wrongly detected as missing.

Define FLB_SYSTEM_QNX when CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME is QNX, add the two libraries to
CMAKE_REQUIRED_LIBRARIES before any probe runs, and link them for every
target. Other systems are unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Jake Hoffman <122403457+jakethehoffer@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 78ab87c..13f92b7 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -41,6 +41,15 @@ if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Darwin")
   add_definitions(-DFLB_SYSTEM_MACOS)
 endif()
 
+# Define macro to identify QNX Neutrino (SDP 8.0)
+if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "QNX")
+  set(FLB_SYSTEM_QNX On)
+  add_definitions(-DFLB_SYSTEM_QNX)
+  # BSD sockets live in libsocket and inotify in libfsnotify on QNX
+  list(APPEND CMAKE_REQUIRED_LIBRARIES socket fsnotify)
+  link_libraries(socket fsnotify)
+endif()
+
 # Define macro to identify Linux system
 if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Linux")
   set(FLB_SYSTEM_LINUX On)
